<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aelia Eudoxia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 404</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aelia Eudoxia (died 404) was the wife of the eastern Roman emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadius">Arcadius</a>, whom she married in 395. The daughter of the Frankish general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bauto">Bauto</a>, she was proclaimed augusta in 400 and became a powerful figure at the court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. Her conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> John Chrysostom led to his exile; she was the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-ii">Theodosius II</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aelia-eudoxia.jpg" alt="Aelia Eudoxia" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aelia_Eudoxia_solidus_(obverse).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
